title: Change order form for electricians (free PDF) | Jobchit
description: A free, printable electrician change-order form. Record added circuits, panel or service changes, wire and breaker sizes, permit or inspection changes, the new total and both signatures. No account needed.
heading: Change order for electricians
sub: For an added circuit, a panel or service change, or a fixture swap the customer asks for after the job starts. Write down the extra work and get both signatures before it starts.
tips:
  - Name the room or panel location so the customer knows exactly where the extra work will happen.
  - Write the circuit details: breaker size, wire gauge and type, and the approximate run length. Say which loads the circuit will serve.
  - Note any panel or service work, such as a new sub-panel or an upgraded service, and who pulls the permit.
  - Record the fixtures, devices or equipment being added and who supplies them. Keep photos of the existing panel with the job record.
  - Both sides sign and date it before the extra work starts. Give the customer a copy.
  - Some states have their own rules for change orders. Check with your state licensing board.
